# API Contract Rules

- All feature APIs use `/api/v1`.
- Define request/response DTOs before platform implementation.
- Use typed success/error responses consistent with the existing API envelope.
- Validate every externally supplied value.
- Map backend errors to stable client-facing error codes/messages.
- Never expose stack traces or internal exception details.
- Authentication, authorization and ownership are enforced server-side.
- Use correlation/request IDs.
- Retry only operations that are safe to retry.
- Use idempotency for operations explicitly requiring it, especially checkout/payment/shipping/refund flows.
- Keep API changes backward-compatible unless the sprint explicitly requires a breaking change.
- Update API documentation/OpenAPI when contracts change.
